      "committedDate": "2026-10-01T07:10:33Z",
      "messageBody": "Apply consistent naming pattern: bug-fixer-{domain}-loop for sidecars,\nbug-fixer-{domain} for skills.\n\nSidecar renames (directory names):\n  - bug-fixer-tick       → bug-fixer-engineering-loop\n  - bug-fixer-triage     → bug-fixer-triage-loop\n  - bug-fixer-architect  → bug-fixer-pr-review-loop\n  - trajectory-review    → bug-fixer-trajectory-loop\n\nSkill renames (directory names):\n  - bug-fixer-tick       → bug-fixer-engineering\n  - trajectory-review    → bug-fixer-trajectory-review\n\nDisplay names (UI-facing, no '-loop' suffix):\n  - Bug Fixer Tick       → Bug Fixer Engineering\n  - Bug Fixer Architect Review → Bug Fixer PR Review\n  - Bug Fixer Triage     → (unchanged)\n  - Bug Fixer Trajectory Review → (unchanged)\n\nRationale:\n  - Sidecars are the loop/mechanism; skills are the role/capability\n  - '-loop' suffix disambiguates sidecar from skill when domain names match\n  - UI display names drop '-loop' since the Scheduled Tasks context is sufficient\n  - 'bug-fixer-' prefix on all names for consistent grouping\n  - Domain describes what the loop processes, not who does the work\n\nAlso adds architect_cron config key and backward-compatible cleanup in uninstall.sh.",
